@startuml tick_path
title CPU tick -> BAC -> IBPU -> FTQ -> Fetch: integration order
hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 95

legend left
  [E] Existing gem5 call or signal
  [N] New IBPU / bridge / helper connection
  [A] Model algorithm; illustrative private operation
  Dashed arrows are returns; time-buffer writes are not direct callbacks.
endlegend

participant "gem5 event queue" as Events
participant "o3::CPU" as CPU
participant "o3::BAC" as BAC
participant "Gem5BpuBridge" as Bridge
participant "selected IBPU" as BPU
participant "o3::FTQ" as FTQ
participant "o3::Fetch" as Fetch
participant "Decode / Rename / IEW / Commit" as Stages
participant "O3 time buffers" as TB

note over CPU, BAC
  Sources: cpu.cc CPU::tick() (368), bac.cc BAC::tick() (503),
  BAC::checkSignalsAndUpdate() (375),
  BAC::checkAndUpdateBPUSignals() (290).
  Scope: decoupledFrontEnd = true, with custom or legacy BPU.
  [N] arrows describe a proposed implementation, not existing C++.
  Insert mode dispatch INSIDE the existing feedback method:
  IBPU forwarding replaces legacy bpu update/squash calls.
  Drain history cleanup in checkSignalsAndUpdate uses the same dispatch.
end note

Events -> CPU : [E] tickEvent -> CPU::tick()
CPU -> CPU : [E] update cycle counters
CPU -> BAC : [E] tick()
loop each active thread (current decoupled mode supports one thread)
    BAC -> BAC : [E] checkSignalsAndUpdate(tid)
    BAC -> BAC : [E] checkAndUpdateBPUSignals(tid)
    BAC -> TB : [E] read fromCommit / fromDecode / fromFetch wires
    TB --> BAC : [E] signals visible after configured backward delays
    alt bpuModel is configured
        BAC -> Bridge : [N] forwardFeedback(timeBuffer)
        ref over Bridge, BPU
          commit_update.puml / backend_recovery.puml
          commit squash wins; otherwise commit frontier update,
          then decode squash, then fetch repair
        end ref
        BAC -> FTQ : [E] isReady / isLocked / isFull / numFreeEntries
        FTQ --> BAC : [E] current queue status and free entries
        BAC -> BAC : [N] build credits and admission permission
        BAC -> Bridge : [N] service(curCycle(), credits)
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] tick(now, credits)
        ref over BPU
          bpu_lookahead.puml
          progress due work, validate forecast, schedule permitted issues
        end ref
        BPU --> Bridge : [N] due data/control events available
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] peekOverride(now)
        alt an override event is due (validate stale events too)
            ref over Bridge, Fetch
              mbtb_late_recover.puml
              apply local correction or await O3 recovery arbitration
            end ref
        end
        alt admission allowed and no unresolved affected-path recovery
            ref over Bridge, FTQ
              ftq request.puml
              peek -> insert -> accept, bounded by current credits
            end ref
        else FTQ full/locked, draining or recovery pending
            Bridge -> Bridge : [A] skip affected data admission; keep due work alive
        end
        Bridge -> BPU : [N] nextWakeup()
        BPU --> Bridge : [N] optional future cycle deadline
        Bridge -> CPU : [N] arrange model wakeup (lifecycle.puml)
        Bridge --> BAC : [N] service complete; report current activity
    else legacy configuration
        note over BAC
          Existing BPredUnit update/squash calls remain inside
          checkAndUpdateBPUSignals(). Do not also invoke IBPU.
        end note
        opt bacStatus == Running
            BAC -> BAC : [E] generateFetchTargets(tid, status_change)
            BAC -> FTQ : [E] insert(tid, curFT)
        end
    end
end
BAC -> BAC : [E] updateBACStatus() when status changes
opt activity occurred
    BAC -> CPU : [E] activityThisCycle()
end
BAC --> CPU : [E] return

CPU -> Fetch : [E] tick()
ref over Fetch, FTQ
  fetch_blocks_merge.puml / predecode_feedback.puml
  queue head -> memory fragments -> decoder -> prediction binding
end ref
Fetch -> TB : [E] write toDecode->insts from fetchQueue (up to decodeWidth)
Fetch --> CPU : [E] return
CPU -> Stages : [E] decode.tick()
opt Decode produces backward information
    Stages -> TB : [E] write decodeInfo / stalls during decode.tick()
end
CPU -> Stages : [E] rename.tick()
opt Rename produces backward information
    Stages -> TB : [E] write stall / unblock signals during rename.tick()
end
CPU -> Stages : [E] iew.tick()
opt IEW produces results or recovery information
    Stages -> TB : [E] write iewQueue / iewInfo during iew.tick()
end
CPU -> Stages : [E] commit.tick()
opt Commit produces retirement / recovery information
    Stages -> TB : [E] write commitInfo during commit.tick()
end
CPU -> TB : [E] timeBuffer.advance(); fetchQueue.advance();
CPU -> TB : [E] decodeQueue.advance(); renameQueue.advance(); iewQueue.advance()
CPU -> CPU : [E] activityRec.advance(); cleanup; next-tick scheduling; tryDrain()

note over BAC, Fetch
  Model service must run even when legacy BAC status is FTQFull.
  FTQ capacity gates admission/new issue, not all pipeline completion.
  BAC precedes Fetch: an admitted head can be seen in this CPU tick.
  A configured publication delay must be reflected in readyCycle;
  the current bacToFetchDelay member does not itself gate FTQ reads.
end note
note over Stages, TB
  Calls occur in the order above, but signals traverse their time buffers.
  A Commit result produced here is not delivered to BAC earlier in this tick.
  Detailed ordering of each source is in backend_recovery.puml.
end note
@enduml
